The [original incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says “One issue, one fix queued”.
Its computed cause table disagrees. The supplied KB describes a shared-parser
problem and a separate booking-form instruction problem, so one parser fix must
not be treated as resolving both.

## What is different

- **Parser:** the shared parser reads numeric dates month-first even when the
  tenant's date convention is day-first. In `R-41203`, an app booking for
  2 December appears in the invite as 12 February.
- **Form hint:** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, but for a day-first tenant its
  form interprets the entry day-first. In `R-41259`, a form booking for 11 April
  appears as 4 November. The visible instruction and interpretation must agree;
  this is not evidence that the shared parser alone caused this report.

These mechanisms come from the supplied KB logic and tenant data. The production
parser and form were not supplied; reproductions against the actual product
remain to be performed. The computed assignment is useful for triage, not proof
that every report individually demonstrates the assigned mechanism.

<ReviewFindings />

